'''3.''' Want of reality; inanity; nihility.
{{smaller block|If they’ll run behind the glass to catch at it, their expectations will meet with ''vacuity'' and emptiness. ''Glanville.''}}
'''4.''' Freedom from mental exertion; thoughtlessness; listlessness; idleness.
{{smaller block|A patient people, much given to slumber and ''vacuity'', and but little troubled with the disease of thinking.
